course: dictionary
lesson: 9911
title: Tam: a cap, a name, and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «In Aberdeen, Nell has invented two brothers, Rab and Tam, who get blamed for every mess.» Brothers have names, and Tam has a capital letter, so here Tam is a name.
explain: A tam is a soft, round, flat woollen cap, often with a bobble on top. It is traditionally worn in Scotland. If a sentence is about a cap in a Scottish story, tam is probably the cap. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Tam can also be a short form of a longer name, such as Thomas. When you meet tam, ask yourself: does the sentence need a person's name, or a hat?
fact: A tam is a noun: one tam, two tams.
fact: A tam is a soft, round, flat woollen cap, often with a bobble (pom-pom) on top.
fact: Tam is short for tam-o'-shanter, the Scottish cap.
fact: Tam can also be a short form of the name Thomas or Tamsin.
fact: In Ukrainian, «tam» (там) means «there», said like «tum». It is not an English word in that sense.
exercise: «In Aberdeen, Nell has invented two brothers, Rab and Tam, who get blamed for every mess.» In this sentence, what is Tam? | A petrol station | The word for there | A soft woollen cap | *A name for one of the brothers
exercise: What is a tam? | A bobble for a bag | A kind of petrol | *A soft, round, flat woollen cap | A Scottish dinner
exercise: In Ukrainian, «tam» means what? | A hat | Here | *There | Tomorrow
test: Tam is a short form of which longer name? | *Thomas | Tank | Tower | Tim
test: What is a soft, round, flat woollen cap with a bobble called? | *A tam | A glen | A kilt | A servo
exam: What is the best way to find the meaning of tam when you are not sure? | Look only at the capital letters | Skip the sentence and never come back | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Guess the first meaning you think of
